<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:38Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-eu" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1433?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ukraine's bid for NATO membership and more air defense remains controversial</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:938570d904ba11c6aa652ccb94094092bf31e67f1ab7aa6fd411aa5a88ff47c6</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T16:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-bid-for-nato-membership-and-more-air-defense-remains-controversial/a-80029852--1abf02560b4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-bid-for-nato-membership-and-more-air-defense-remains-controversial/a-80029852?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy is calling for the rapid acceptance of his country into NATO. However, the necessary unanimity for this is lacking, as shown during the NATO Parliamentary Assembly in Berlin.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU enlargement: Why do some EU member states use their vetoes to block the accession of certain candidate countries?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:759629e809550c7b4665b6933a932d44a62e38f956cbfd3d2c7abd62041d0cf6</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-why-do-some-eu-member-states-use-their-vetoes-to-block-the-accession-of-certain-candi/a-80034401--27cd622204d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-why-do-some-eu-member-states-use-their-vetoes-to-block-the-accession-of-certain-candidate-countries/a-80034401?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Individual EU member states use their veto powers to block candidate countries in the accession process — often for reasons of domestic politics. DW takes a look at some cases and examines what's behind them.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Macedonia remains stalled on its EU path after 21 years as a candidate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20a23bcccce93f53e3b03368056210a62f46af5caa1da862f2344076ce493b6b</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T13:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-macedonia-remains-stalled-on-its-eu-path-after-21-years-as-a-candidate/a-80020841--291e539f1390.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-macedonia-remains-stalled-on-its-eu-path-after-21-years-as-a-candidate/a-80020841?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU enlargement has regained momentum, with Montenegro and Albania moving closer to membership. But North Macedonia, a candidate since 2005, remains stalled by a politically difficult dispute involving Bulgaria.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German police respond to multiple school bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f1fab8589ed177003a526d7c9621d4e93492fb2748c99fb3d4a0fed733eb7f4</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T11:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-respond-to-multiple-school-bomb-threats/a-80018842--56ba1301d92a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-respond-to-multiple-school-bomb-threats/a-80018842?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police in Germany are responding to bomb threats against a series of schools, but say that at present they don't believe them to be credible. Danish authorities are reporting a similar series of apparent hoaxes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian helicopter suspected of violating Finnish airspace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:14bb147736dad0c076f157c1539bedb328f045def70c77c3f5fdb645dc5178aa</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T17:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-helicopter-suspected-of-violating-finnish-airspace/a-80010133--74b233a91706.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-helicopter-suspected-of-violating-finnish-airspace/a-80010133?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finland's Defense Ministry thinks the incursion is linked to a drone strike earlier Saturday on a Russian cargo ship, which is on a US sanctions list.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU and Indonesia sign trade deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a1bc5ad3c6f41ea2ba1a6c1640b0c1adb2583754c3d59f6df8adac6d8fb93a4</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T15:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-and-indonesia-sign-trade-deal/a-80010099--bb068ad239d4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-and-indonesia-sign-trade-deal/a-80010099?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A deal covering 730 million people promises lower tariffs and new investment opportunities as the European Union seeks to diversify trade ties amid growing global economic tensions.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU takes aim at tech giants in tax proposal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d90e7c311c54695d4afd91609daa13303f6a642370f0ff34f037c84f1b9fb62d</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T14:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-takes-aim-at-tech-giants-in-tax-proposal/a-80009255--1b2179c47506.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-takes-aim-at-tech-giants-in-tax-proposal/a-80009255?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">European Council President Antonio Costa has proposed a smaller EU budget for 2028-2034, including a 3% tax on major digital firms to ease member states' contributions. France has already rejected the plan as inadequate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia strikes Zelenskyy's hometown, killing 2</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:251a7d7b5c257237af32e2dcca34efd95e82de76c99dc96108c0b81d43c6c5dc</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T14:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-strikes-zelenskyy-s-hometown-killing-2/a-80009458--1c5b88d83c35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-strikes-zelenskyy-s-hometown-killing-2/a-80009458?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The attacks follow Russian President Vladimir Putin's vow of a "painful" response to Ukraine's attacks this week on the Kerch Bridge, linking Russian-occupied Crimea.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian ornithologist jailed over small donations to Navalny's foundation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c39e259b769dd99c2a3c0291d666a14494a32137a0f2d72ce40fb16668022dab</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-ornithologist-jailed-over-small-donations-to-navalny-s-foundation/a-80005505--49dba4e1f94e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-ornithologist-jailed-over-small-donations-to-navalny-s-foundation/a-80005505?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sofia Rosenfeld has devoted her life to studying Arctic birds. A Russian court sentenced her to 3.5 years in a penal colony over donations to Navalny's foundation. Friends and family are fighting for her release.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU and UK strike 'landmark deal' to strengthen ties after Brexit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:738f77cda6b149beea1bbf79b44b1a1ca602726076587ce51880c58571912f0e</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-and-uk-strike-landmark-deal-to-strengthen-ties-after-brexit/a-80001076--f12586fcea84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-and-uk-strike-landmark-deal-to-strengthen-ties-after-brexit/a-80001076?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union and the United Kingdom have agreed on "landmark" deals on youth mobility and trade. Leaders on both sides praised the agreement as they seek to rebuild ties.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey takes control of opposition broadcaster Sozcu TV</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbcb464ced9c36b30289e8b01ed831842c46676ecacac7f59cab62e57a6a183a</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-takes-control-of-opposition-broadcaster-sozcu-tv/a-80001984--d9f6e0119d22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-takes-control-of-opposition-broadcaster-sozcu-tv/a-80001984?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In the latest in a series of raids and arrests, another major pro-opposition Turkish broadcaster has been brought under state control. This is the third in a year.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Putin proposes second humanitarian ceasefire — is it a trap?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:525b4d33b2abcbec8d84ffbcd99ceb285b92bc96b38cbe2fb6b5eef6be18cb5e</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T20:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/putin-proposes-second-humanitarian-ceasefire-is-it-a-trap/a-79996772--e715071e3f54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/putin-proposes-second-humanitarian-ceasefire-is-it-a-trap/a-79996772?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian President Putin has suggested evacuating civilians from the embattled Ukrainian city of Kostiantynivka. But experts warn this could serve military, not humanitarian, aims. What should Kyiv do?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU Commission confirms it was targeted in cyberattack using AI tools</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b914c018f8191193e031cfe5cfaf8a3e6a287529bd05090c824093f2f571410</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T14:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-commission-confirms-it-was-targeted-in-cyberattack-using-ai-tools/a-79993016--2e1cd85b257c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-commission-confirms-it-was-targeted-in-cyberattack-using-ai-tools/a-79993016?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission was targeted by an "AI-generated cybercampaign," a spokesperson has said. This is the first time the bloc has publicly reported an AI-based cyberattack.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wadephul: 'Coalition of the Willing' talks in Berlin send strong signal to Moscow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f92e4a805fc1d3925ed2d907ad8a93be351b777794bb101d77072adbab837522</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wadephul-coalition-of-the-willing-talks-in-berlin-send-strong-signal-to-moscow/a-79990664--ce1ce93ebd6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wadephul-coalition-of-the-willing-talks-in-berlin-send-strong-signal-to-moscow/a-79990664?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Foreign Minister Wadephul has said the Coalition of the Willing meeting in Berlin sends a clear message to Moscow to take peace talks seriously. He also warned Ukraine should be prepared for peace talks to fail.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hashim Thaci's second conviction in The Hague reignites debate in Kosovo about justice and the Kosovo Specialist Chambers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e014b7423cb38cff310322751cc3c2f0d630cd9bf5362d346f4f31754d33b0fe</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T20:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hashim-thaci-s-second-conviction-in-the-hague-reignites-debate-in-kosovo-about-justice-and-the-kosov/a-79975227--3db3936546e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hashim-thaci-s-second-conviction-in-the-hague-reignites-debate-in-kosovo-about-justice-and-the-kosovo-specialist-chambers/a-79975227?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former President Hashim Thaci has been convicted of trying to influence witnesses in his war crimes trial. The conviction has reignited debate in Kosovo about the Kosovo Specialist Chambers, the court that convicted him.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Back to 1997: Russia wants NATO to roll back its eastern expansion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09d71c53aec2e6ab32f8bce0df536743f646c3819dc4fe015fdd950289c5e3a0</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T16:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/back-to-1997-russia-wants-nato-to-roll-back-its-eastern-expansion/a-79970289--e5e38f4e75de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/back-to-1997-russia-wants-nato-to-roll-back-its-eastern-expansion/a-79970289?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Kremlin is reportedly calling on NATO to withdraw from large parts of Eastern Europe. What this would mean for the security of millions of Europeans — and what lies behind Russia's plan.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Rights court rules Turkey must release jailed lawmaker Atalay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8996862f039e765b18e6114dfc2e33228b35d4f4edd6757a365f328e5e285ef8</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T15:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rights-court-rules-turkey-must-release-jailed-lawmaker-atalay/a-79972462--8247972e6110.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rights-court-rules-turkey-must-release-jailed-lawmaker-atalay/a-79972462?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Court of Human Rights has called for the release of imprisoned elected lawmaker Can Atalay. Atalay has been in prison for almost five years despite rulings from the Turkish Constitutional Court.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Students' List candidates take seats as Serbian parliament opens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b76dc6148e2d6dede8041ad955c818a088a74c537310cec4a92a4751b48a76b</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T12:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/students-list-candidates-take-seats-as-serbian-parliament-opens/a-79969166--96de93cfad7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/students-list-candidates-take-seats-as-serbian-parliament-opens/a-79969166?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Serbia's Student List's candidates have taken their oaths in the inaugural parliament session. As the new majority, they have 90 days to form a government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Despite restrictive abortion laws, Poland's 'Abortomat' — a locker that dispenses abortion pills — helps women who want to end a pregnancy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f100b3ba3cbce90987d6fb0799336d04a1f03582342b0e8080361f2c486e7d9</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/polish-activists-face-opposition-as-they-make-abortion-more-accessible/a-79943914--39db4083c558.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/despite-restrictive-abortion-laws-poland-s-abortomat-a-locker-that-dispenses-abortion-pills-helps-women-who-want-to-end-a-pregnancy/a-79943914?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Abortion laws in Poland are very restrictive. Activists there have found a new way to help women wanting to terminate a pregnancy: the "Abortomat," a locker that dispenses abortion pills. But they face fierce opposition.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Zelenskyy says security deal could go to referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:185a8a7cb76437d8ed9bbadf32ef11edf8c53604936ff387803751756eafa700</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-says-security-deal-could-go-to-referendum/a-79947535--17ea05d7ca0f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-says-security-deal-could-go-to-referendum/a-79947535?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US has broached the idea of Kyiv giving up the Donbas region in exchange for NATO membership, the Ukrainian president said.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
